{
  "case_id": "2007-06-571",
  "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nKARL J. KOCH, ESQ., Baton Rouge, La.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nDEANNE E. MAYNARD, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Watson's receipt of a firearm in exchange for drugs does not constitute the use of that firearm as the word \"use\" is employed by 18 U.S.C. Section 924(c)(1) for two principal reasons. First, applying the plain and ordinary meaning of the word \"use,\" the receipt of a thing is not the use of that thing. There is no grammatically proper way to say that someone uses a firearm when all that person does is receive it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, if we look at this transaction, a guns-for-drugs transaction, is there -- can you think of any good reason why Congress would want to prescribe a 5-year penalty for the person who hands over the gun, but not any penalty for the person who receives the gun and hands over the drugs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do think that there are distinctions between the two conducts, sir. First of all, certainly the person that -- that has the gun and is bringing it into that transaction I would suggest, as a practical matter presents a different type of risk."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Perhaps. But it seems to me to unduly constrict the case to say that all he did was receive it. He did more than that. He agreed in advance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BREYER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you have besides the linguistic argument? I mean, when I start out, I can't think of a reason why Congress wouldn't want to penalize the buyer, not the seller."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KOCH",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under Bailey, however, if all he did was receive the gun, hold it in his hand, Bailey says that's not enough, that's not a use. And, of course, those are the facts of this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. MAYNARD",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner used the firearm by accepting it in exchange for his drugs. In doing so Petitioner used it during and in relation to a drug trafficking crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SOUTER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But that does not answer the question use by whom. As I understand it, we are not really arguing about whether the gun was used in the transaction; we are arguing about whether the defendant was the one who used it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. MAYNARD",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think one can employ use in a natural way to mean receipt in the way that Petitioner used the firearm here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have the negotiated transaction where he received the firearms as the medium of exchange."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying that the parties are viewed collectively so that in Justice Breyer's example the pitcher and the batter used a ball and a bat. Is that your position? And in this case the seller and the buyer used drugs and a gun."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is no different. The Court has already held that using the firearm as currency is a violation of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the prosecution would certainly want to assure the success of the argument; and if this is clearly possession, why wasn't possession charged? And does the Department of Justice give any guidance to prosecutors since the 1988 amendment on what to charge in these situations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's hard to say it's in furtherance of the crime when the crime is over once he gets it. His possession is not in furtherance of the crime, it seems to me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I just -- I don't understand the significance of the argument you just made. Are you saying that because some people might be let out of prison if we correctly construed the statute, we should read it your way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "From now on, the government could charge, if you rule against us in this case, we believe we can charge this conduct under possession and furtherance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eff1f73fbf70d37f69a699155e1e416cb7820f54c7a7a0e00cefa7bc130e9e77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eff1f73fbf70-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For example, in the First Circuit's decision in Cotto, which is currently pending before the Court, the -- the person who ultimately came -- became the confidential informant -- before that the drug deal her sold to her drugs for guns on 20 separate occasions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-571",
      "confidence": 0.0,
